# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations. Non-gating — a report,
#            not a gate (see Mustfile for hard gates).
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done | deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#
# NOTE (2026-06-13): rewritten for Cliometrics.jl. The file the estate branch
# carried was the un-substituted rsr-template-repo Intentfile (its intents
# were "repo-initialization / contractile-completeness for the template").

@abstract:
North-star for Cliometrics.jl: quantitative economic history in Julia.
Applies econometric and statistical methods to historical economic phenomena —
growth accounting, convergence analysis, institutional quality measurement,
and counterfactual modeling — with a Zig FFI layer for performance-critical
data paths and Documenter.jl docs.
@end

## Purpose

Cliometrics.jl provides Julia tools for quantitative economic history:
- Historical data loading and cleaning (CSV, interpolation, gap-filling)
- Growth accounting: Solow residual / TFP decomposition
- Convergence analysis (beta-convergence, half-life calculations)
- Institutional quality indices (composite with custom weights)
- Counterfactual / treatment-effect estimation (DiD)
- Zig FFI layer for performance-critical data paths (ffi/)

## Anti-Purpose

Cliometrics.jl is NOT:
- a general economics simulation framework
- a replacement for full econometrics packages (StatsModels, etc.)
- a real-time or live-data pipeline (batch/historical data only)
- a web service or API server

## If In Doubt

Sensitive areas — ask before changing: `src/Cliometrics.jl` (main module
logic), `ffi/` (Zig FFI ABI), `Project.toml` (dependency pinning),
`.claude/CLAUDE.md`.

